{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"b5846eae7879a0289e577bf5c3019cf394792c01282846305c2cfad757fea555","digest":{"component_or_area":"op-cert service configuration","key_entities":["REBAR_OPCERT_PRIVATE_KEY","OpcertServiceConfig.from_env","src/rebar/opcert_service/config.py","_private_key_env","compose_signer","keyprov._validate_key_file","workspace._git","REBAR_OPCERT_KEY_PATH"],"problem_keywords":["credential hygiene","environment variable exposure","inline PEM","secret management","subprocess inheritance"],"propositions":["REBAR_OPCERT_PRIVATE_KEY environment variable remains in os.environ after OpcertServiceConfig.from_env reads it, leaking the inline PEM to child processes (ssh-keygen, git) and environment dumps","The inline PEM secret is inherited by subprocess.run calls that do not explicitly pass env, exposing the key to ssh-keygen and git commands spawned by the service","OpcertServiceConfig.from_env should consume the REBAR_OPCERT_PRIVATE_KEY variable via pop rather than copy, removing it from os.environ after transfer to the config object","A second call to OpcertServiceConfig.from_env in the same process must yield private_key=None without error, enforcing consume-once semantics and preventing silent regression if reload paths are added later"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787370951455316001,"uuid":"bbab261f-2d64-416c-a1ee-d6375533cca6"}